# Intent: Train 6 item 1, offline phrases on the unit (legacy patch 118 rebuilt on the Train 4 tree). When the wake word or a tap finds no link to Home, the unit says one short clip for the state it knows instead of only the tone: no Wi-Fi, connecting (Home has not answered for under 10 s), Home not answering (10 s or more), or refused (Home accepted the connection and closed it before its hello, twice in a row; counted in the reconnect loop, never for a host that is merely slow). "I'm back" plays after a long outage that sounded the 3 minute offline tone. Sixteen clips in five groups (the files of host/maipai_body/bodies/stackchan/firmware/assets/phrases), embedded in the app image as flash data (about 60 KB, memory mapped: no RAM, no task, no timer). The choice is the pure core already in maipai_sounds_core.h (ms_phrase_pick): never the same clip twice in a row, at most one per 10 s and three in any minute, then the old tone; at night or with sounds switched off the tone only; muted, nothing; a clip that is not in the image falls back to the tone and is counted. The wake and stop checks are untouched: the hook replaces the one tone call of ShowCantReachHome, which runs after the wake word has already fired, and no audio path, task or stack changes. Tool self.audio.offline_phrase (bench: a dry run reads the embedded clip and decides on a copy of the limits, ignoring the mute, night and sounds-off choice); self.audio.sound_info now reports clips_present, clips_played and clips_missing.
# Placement: unit (the phrases are said by the robot with the host off; the host's own tier 1 line is for a body that is up with Home down: the two never both speak, because this runs only when the unit has no socket to the host)
# Upstream: firmware/xiaozhi-esp32 application.cc and websocket_protocol.cc (MIT); legacy MaiPai patch 118. The clips are the household's default synthetic voice (no recording of a person); a different voice is a data swap of the 16 files, no code.
# Check after a flash: self.audio.sound_info reports clips_present 16; self.audio.offline_phrase with dry true answers kind clip, a group name, a variant and the clip's byte count for each of no_wifi, no_host, refused, connecting and back; with the hub stopped for 20 s the wake word says a no_host clip (and a different one the next time, at most one per 10 s); a muted unit says nothing; at night the tone only.
# Kconfig: MAIPAI_OFFLINE_PHRASES (default y); off embeds nothing and the wake path plays the old tone only. The build stops with a plain message when it is on and the clip files are not found (source scripts/fw-env.sh sets MAIPAI_PHRASES_DIR).
